# SRG-APP-000120-AU-000120  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must protect audit information from unauthorized
# deletion.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000120-AU-000120
group:           V-221916
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000164
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Splunk keeps audit records from being removed through the product by
                 withholding the delete capability from the general-purpose roles and by
                 keeping the internal indexes out of every role's delete scope.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [role_user] delete_by_keyword absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] delete_by_keyword absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_can_delete] deleteIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|;)[[:space:]]*_
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] deleteIndexesAllowed matches tls1\.2 -> authorize.conf [role_can_delete] deleteIndexesAllowed not_matches (^|;)[[:space:]]*_
vendor:          authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] deleteIndexesAllowed https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/authorize.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Delete permissions on the index bucket files on disk - SPLK-CL-000190
                 implements this with splunk-user ownership and mode 700 at the operating
                 system layer
external:        Which roles the organization authorizes to run the delete command

citation:        Three corrections. deleteIndexesAllowed not_in *|_* carries the wildcard
                 inversion corrected on SRG-APP-000119-AU-000110. frozenTimePeriodInSecs
                 present cannot fail - indexes.conf.spec:691 gives a default of 188697600,
                 so btool reports the key on every index. coldToFrozenDir non_empty fails a
                 stock install (indexes.conf.spec:792-802 makes the archive destination an
                 alternative to a script, and neither the check text nor SPLK-CL-000190
                 asks for one) and tests the wrong thing: rolling to frozen is authorized
                 retention behavior, not unauthorized deletion. Retention belongs to
                 SRG-APP-000125-AU-000310 and SRG-APP-000365-AU-000210, where it is
                 assessed. source_of_value moves from organization_defined to spec_default
                 because the conditions now rest on the shipped role model, not on an
                 organization's number.
finding:         A general-purpose role holds delete_by_keyword, or a role's
                 deleteIndexesAllowed list reaches the internal indexes, so audit records
                 can be removed from search results by an unprivileged account.
